WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:19.769
Zann blurted out as the faint voice and the pain finally disappeared.

2
00:00:20.589 --> 00:00:23.270
"That was the weirdest Share I've ever had."

3
00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.371
He was worried about Boz and the other Reds back at his house.

4
00:00:28.331 --> 00:00:30.152
What if something had happened after he'd left?

5
00:00:31.124 --> 00:00:34.527
Zann grabbed Zing and zapped back to his family's dining room.

6
00:00:39.451 --> 00:00:40.972
His father smiled brightly at him.

7
00:00:40.992 --> 00:00:42.093
"You're back, Zann."

8
00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:47.318
"Yep." Zann glanced around, relieved to see that everyone seemed to be okay.

9
00:00:47.338 --> 00:00:49.560
"Is everything all right here?"

10
00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.041
"Of course."

11
00:00:51.281 --> 00:00:53.123
Teplo reached for the puckerberry pudding.

12
00:00:53.143 --> 00:00:57.766
"Except that we're running out of dessert."

13
00:00:57.846 --> 00:00:59.288
Most of the other adults chuckled.

14
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.221
But Boz stared at Zann.

15
00:01:02.061 --> 00:01:03.422
"What's the matter, my boy?"

16
00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:04.222
he asked.

17
00:01:04.242 --> 00:01:07.363
"You look as agitated as a panic bug."

18
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:11.585
"Something strange just happened," Zann said.

19
00:01:12.606 --> 00:01:14.566
He told the adults about the Red Share.

20
00:01:14.586 --> 00:01:18.708
"That is odd," Saffa said when Zann finished.

21
00:01:18.728 --> 00:01:23.810
"If the Share didn't come from any of us, it must have come from another Red whom you

22
00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.472
know." Boz stood up and rubbed his fingers together.

23
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:29.841
"We should check around.

24
00:01:30.121 --> 00:01:30.901
Just in case."

25
00:01:30.921 --> 00:01:35.283
"Don't worry, though, Zann," Nax said.

26
00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:40.245
"The close presence of so many powerful relics could be causing this.

27
00:01:41.386 --> 00:01:47.088
Their energy has been interfering with all magic energy, especially for Reds, who are more sensitive to magic."

28
00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:49.450
Zann nodded slowly.

29
00:01:52.551 --> 00:01:54.532
He wanted to believe his father was right.

30
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.883
But he couldn't help remembering how desperate that faint voice had sounded.

31
00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.548
That night Zann had trouble falling asleep.

32
00:02:06.589 --> 00:02:10.372
He stared at the ceiling, still thinking about that weird Red Share.

33
00:02:11.353 --> 00:02:12.874
Who was trying to contact him?

34
00:02:14.155 --> 00:02:19.159
Boz and the others had checked with most of the Reds they knew, and so far everyone was

35
00:02:19.219 --> 00:02:20.801
fine. Tap!

36
00:02:20.841 --> 00:02:24.744
Tap! Zann sat up when he heard a light rapping on his window.

37
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.281
A spy fly fluttered outside.

38
00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:29.982
Zann was confused.

39
00:02:30.542 --> 00:02:33.063
Spy flies usually stayed hidden while spying.

40
00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:40.706
But this one was trying to get his attention.

41
00:02:41.907 --> 00:02:44.628
After hesitating a moment, Zann opened the window.

42
00:02:46.388 --> 00:02:49.610
He gasped as the spy fly dived straight into his ear.

43
00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:51.650
"What's going on?"

44
00:02:51.991 --> 00:02:52.511
Zann thought.

45
00:02:52.531 --> 00:02:55.092
"I didn't summon a spy fly."

46
00:02:55.996 --> 00:03:01.678
Suddenly an image filled his mind, and in it he saw his three best friends!

47
00:03:01.698 --> 00:03:03.899
"Hi, Zann!"

48
00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.440
Perda waved, looking pleased with herself.

49
00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:10.442
"If this works, you should be seeing all of us right now."

50
00:03:11.363 --> 00:03:12.203
Gliss grinned.

51
00:03:12.223 --> 00:03:16.505
"Yes, Perda is still trying to invent new kinds of magic.

52
00:03:16.965 --> 00:03:18.966
Like tinkering with spy flies."

53
00:03:20.146 --> 00:03:21.727
Zann could hardly believe it.

54
00:03:22.247 --> 00:03:24.108
Seeing his friends was great!

55
00:03:25.236 --> 00:03:29.118
"Hi, guys," he murmured, even though he knew they couldn't hear him.

56
00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:32.500
Suddenly he felt more homesick than ever.

57
00:03:33.661 --> 00:03:37.783
His friends chatted for a while, filling him in on all the news around Swamp Bottom.

58
00:03:38.723 --> 00:03:43.726
They even mentioned that Jev had moved away, though none of them knew where he'd gone.

59
00:03:43.746 --> 00:03:47.748
"I know where he is," Zann thought with a sick feeling.

60
00:03:48.729 --> 00:03:50.350
But he didn't think about Jev for long.

61
00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.871
He was more interested in listening to his friends.

62
00:03:54.476 --> 00:03:57.178
"Okay, we should send the fly off now," Darb said at last.

63
00:03:58.079 --> 00:03:58.779
Gliss nodded.

64
00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:02.422
"We haven't figured out how to get there for your birthday yet."

65
00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:06.224
"But we'll definitely be there," Perda added.

66
00:04:07.425 --> 00:04:10.167
"Even if we have to take a wormhole to First City!"

67
00:04:10.187 --> 00:04:15.111
"I'm sure that won't be necessary," Gliss said with a shudder.

68
00:04:15.131 --> 00:04:19.594
"Although Perda has been studying up on the vortex lately!"

69
00:04:20.735 --> 00:04:21.916
Zann felt alarmed.

70
00:04:22.976 --> 00:04:26.318
Perda was bold enough to do something crazy like jump into a wormhole.

71
00:04:27.138 --> 00:04:28.439
He'd been the same way once.

72
00:04:28.739 --> 00:04:31.120
But he had a healthy respect for the vortex these days.

73
00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.161
The spy fly wiggled out of Zann's ear.

74
00:04:35.261 --> 00:04:40.464
Zann didn't know how to get it to spy on him and return to the three kids, though

75
00:04:40.484 --> 00:04:41.824
he planned to ask Perda.

76
00:04:43.985 --> 00:04:47.587
So he summoned a message moth and inscribed a quick note to his friends.

77
00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:53.194
Then he fell asleep, thinking about good old Swamp Bottom.

78
00:04:56.556 --> 00:05:01.059
Zap. Zann landed across the street from the Academy the next morning.

79
00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.441
Several people raced toward him.

80
00:05:03.461 --> 00:05:07.084
"Red!" one shouted, sounding angry.

81
00:05:07.104 --> 00:05:09.265
"We don't want your kind here."

82
00:05:10.306 --> 00:05:13.889
Zann realized he'd landed in the middle of yet another protest.

83
00:05:13.909 --> 00:05:15.990
"Leave me alone!"

84
00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:16.911
Zann exclaimed.

85
00:05:17.271 --> 00:05:17.932
"I'm leaving."

86
00:05:18.912 --> 00:05:22.454
He snapped his fingers to zap across the street and into the school.

87
00:05:23.415 --> 00:05:27.118
But instead he landed on his rear end right in front of the door.

88
00:05:27.138 --> 00:05:33.502
"Drat," he muttered, remembering that the Academy had a special kind of Shield spell over it.

89
00:05:34.603 --> 00:05:38.785
The shield was there to prevent kids from zapping in or out during the day.

90
00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:44.810
Zann's old school in Swamp Bottom was a lot smaller, so it didn't need that kind of spell.

91
00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.992
Grumbling, he opened the door and hurried inside.

92
00:05:48.992 --> 00:05:50.574
He almost crashed into Mari.

93
00:05:50.594 --> 00:05:52.135
"Hi, Zann!"

94
00:05:52.415 --> 00:05:53.656
She greeted him with a smile.

95
00:05:53.676 --> 00:05:54.857
"Did you just get here?"

96
00:05:54.877 --> 00:05:57.519
"Yes," Zann said.

97
00:05:57.539 --> 00:06:00.042
"I ran into another protest outside."

98
00:06:00.062 --> 00:06:01.783
"I saw that too."

99
00:06:02.204 --> 00:06:03.865
Mari didn't sound very interested.

100
00:06:03.885 --> 00:06:09.270
"Hey, did your parents say anything about my offer to volunteer at their lab?

101
00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:11.251
I really want to do it."

102
00:06:11.271 --> 00:06:14.234
"They didn't say anything to me," Zann said.

103
00:06:14.254 --> 00:06:16.436
"I can remind them if you want.

104
00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:19.198
They're so busy these days that they might have forgotten."

105
00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:20.660
"Could you?

106
00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.001
That would be great!"

107
00:06:22.261 --> 00:06:22.822
Mari said.

108
00:06:22.842 --> 00:06:23.903
"Thanks, Zann."

109
00:06:24.963 --> 00:06:25.944
Zann didn't answer.

110
00:06:25.964 --> 00:06:28.767
He'd just spotted another familiar face.

111
00:06:28.787 --> 00:06:30.949
"What's he doing here?"

112
00:06:31.189 --> 00:06:32.190
he said, annoyed.

113
00:06:33.091 --> 00:06:34.292
Mari followed his gaze.

114
00:06:34.312 --> 00:06:35.633
"You mean Jev?

115
00:06:36.374 --> 00:06:37.375
He just enrolled here."

116
00:06:37.395 --> 00:06:40.858
"Great," Zann said with a sigh.

117
00:06:40.878 --> 00:06:42.780
"That's just great."

118
00:06:45.516 --> 00:06:48.637
That afternoon Zann couldn't wait to escape from school.

119
00:06:49.658 --> 00:06:52.099
Jev had been in all of Zann's classes.

120
00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:57.281
Zann was already tired of his old enemy's sneers and dirty looks.

121
00:07:00.362 --> 00:07:02.323
He hurried outside and took a deep breath.

122
00:07:03.984 --> 00:07:06.545
He rubbed his fingers together to create magic friction.

123
00:07:07.565 --> 00:07:11.527
But before he could zap away, he noticed a message moth flapping toward him.

124
00:07:12.507 --> 00:07:14.028
The message was from his friends.

125
00:07:15.157 --> 00:07:15.898
Zann smiled.

126
00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:17.763
"My friends are coming!"
